  "title": "BNCI2003_IVa Motor Imagery dataset",
  "description": "EEG recordings from five healthy participants performing cued motor imagery (right hand versus foot) with 118 electrodes, originally published to demonstrate improved single-trial classification through feature combination and multiclass paradigms. The data were downsampled to 100 Hz and comprise 280 cued trials per subject, split into labeled training and unlabeled test sets. The dataset was part of BCI Competition III and is widely used for benchmarking BCI classification algorithms.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded with BrainAmp amplifiers from 118 channels, band-pass filtered at 0.05-200 Hz and sampled at 1000 Hz, then downsampled to 100 Hz. Subjects imagined right hand or right foot movement for 3.5 s following a visual cue, with random inter-trial intervals of 1.75-2.25 s.",
